# CodFlow server — local development secrets
# Copy this file to .dev.vars and fill in your values.
# (.dev.vars is gitignored — your real values never get committed.)

# ── Required for local dev ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Used by the storefront (cod-astro) and dashboard to authenticate against the
# server's store API. Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# It is hashed with SHA-256 before storage (see scripts/seed-store.ts).
# STORE_API_KEY=

# Better Auth signing secret — the SAME value must be set on cod-client-astro
# (both workers share the auth D1 tables). Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# ── Media on ImageKit, locally (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Out of the box, local media is kept in the local bucket and served by this
# server (wrangler.toml [vars]). To keep it on your ImageKit account instead
# (ImageKit → Developer options; the private key is a secret):
# MEDIA_HOST=imagekit
# MEDIA_DELIVERY=imagekit
# IMAGEKIT_PUBLIC_KEY=public_…
# IMAGEKIT_PRIVATE_KEY=private_…
# IMAGEKIT_FOLDER=/dev/your-name
# MEDIA_ORIGIN=https://ik.imagekit.io/your_imagekit_id/dev/your-name

# ── Optional overrides ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Overrides the [vars] block in wrangler.toml for local runs if you need to test
# MCP token verification against a live dashboard, or a different environment:
# ENVIRONMENT=development
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:4321/api/auth
# WORKER_SELF_URL=http://localhost:8787/
# WORKER_URL=http://localhost:8787

# ── Telegram App, on a local server ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Telegram calls the server back with the bot's updates (pairing, blocks) and
# cannot reach localhost. Run a tunnel (cloudflared tunnel --url
# http://localhost:8787) and put its https origin here; WORKER_SELF_URL stays
# as it is, since the dashboard's sign-in is checked against it.
# TELEGRAM_UPDATES_ORIGIN=https://<name>.trycloudflare.com

# ── MCP SDK v2 (used by the stateless elicitation + OAuth work) ───────────────
# HMAC key that seals stateless MCP elicitation request state (must be >= 32
# bytes). Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# MCP_REQUEST_STATE_KEY=

# HMAC key shared with the Astro dashboard for MCP OAuth login tickets
# (must be >= 32 bytes). Set the SAME value on cod-client-astro. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# MCP_LOGIN_TICKET_SECRET=

# HMAC key that signs review upload grants (photos and voice notes with
# storefront reviews; must be >= 32 bytes). Without it, reviews are text only.
# Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# REVIEW_UPLOAD_SECRET=

# Cookie-encryption key for the @cloudflare/workers-oauth-provider consent
# flow. Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# (Currently unused by the provider version in use; reserved for future need.)
# COOKIE_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# In production all values are set with `wrangler secret put`, never in code.
